  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg">
        <tei:pb ed="1965" n="23" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg"/>
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="92" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/1" n="1"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>A psalm, a song for the Sabbath day: <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/2" n="2"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>It is good to thank the Lord and to sing praise to Thy Name, O Most High, <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/3" n="3"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>to proclaim Thy kindness in the morning and Thy faithfulness at night, <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/4" n="4"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>on the ten-stringed harp, through meditation on the zither. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/5" n="5"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>For Thou hast gladdened me, O Lord, with Thy deeds, in the works of Thy hands do I exult. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/6" n="6"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>How great are Thy works, O Lord, profound indeed are Thy thoughts. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/7" n="7"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>A simpleton cannot know, nor can a fool understand this, <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/8" n="8"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>when the wicked flourish like grass and all evil-doers blossom forth only to be destroyed for ever. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/9" n="9"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>But Thou art supreme to eternity, O Lord. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/10" n="10"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>Behold Thine enemies, O Lord, behold Thine enemies shall perish, all evil-doers shall scatter. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/11" n="11"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>Then shalt Thou lift up my horn like the unicorn, I am anointed with fresh oil. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/12" n="12"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>Then shall my eye look down upon my adversaries, when evil men rise up against me my ears shall hear. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/13" n="13"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>The righteous shall flourish like the palm, like the cedar on Lebanon shall he grow. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/14" n="14"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>Those planted in the House of the Lord shall blossom forth in the courts of our God. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/15" n="15"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>They will yet be luxuriant in old age, full of sap and fresh will they be, <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/92/16" n="16"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n62.jpg" n="23"/>so as to proclaim that the Lord is upright, my Rock in whom there is no wrong. <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
